================================================================================
CATTLEFEEDAI — OFFICIAL SYSTEM STARTUP COMMANDS
================================================================================

ORDER OF STARTUP:
1. Supabase PostgreSQL (Cloud Database: aws-0-ap-south-1.pooler.supabase.com)
2. FastAPI AI Service (Python 3.10 Virtual Environment on Port 8000)
3. Spring Boot Backend (Java 17/24 / Maven on Port 8080)
4. React Native / Expo Frontend (Metro Bundler on Port 8081)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PREREQUISITE: Set Supabase PostgreSQL Environment Variables
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
In PowerShell:
$env:DATABASE_URL="jdbc:postgresql://aws-0-ap-south-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require"
$env:DATABASE_USERNAME="postgres.fwlcvlbctsuzdqickzdl"
$env:DATABASE_PASSWORD="your_supabase_password"

Database schema with all 16 tables already provisioned in Supabase.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TERMINAL 1 — FastAPI AI Microservice (Port 8000)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Open a new PowerShell terminal and run:

cd d:\CattleFeedAI\ai-service
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --reload

# NOTE: If PowerShell ExecutionPolicy blocks Activate.ps1, run directly without activation:
# cd d:\CattleFeedAI\ai-service
# .\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --reload

Verification:
Visit: http://localhost:8000/health
Or PowerShell: curl http://localhost:8000/health

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TERMINAL 2 — Spring Boot Backend API (Port 8080)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Open a new PowerShell terminal and run:

cd d:\CattleFeedAI\backend\cattle-feed-api
mvn spring-boot:run

Verification:
Swagger UI: http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html
AI Integration Check: http://localhost:8080/api/ai/health

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TERMINAL 3 — React Native / Expo Frontend (Port 8081)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Your Wi-Fi LAN IP is: 10.161.215.78
(A .env file has been created in frontend/cattle-feed-app pointing to http://10.161.215.78:8080)

To start Expo:
cd d:\CattleFeedAI\frontend\cattle-feed-app
npm start

* For Physical Android Phone (Expo Go):
  - Scan the terminal QR code with the Expo Go app on your phone.
  - If you previously had the app open on your phone, shake the phone and tap "Reload" (or press 'r' in the terminal) so it picks up the backend URL.
  - On the login screen, tap "Register New Account" at the bottom to create your farmer account.

* For Web Browser:
  - Either press 'w' inside the running npm start terminal
  - Or in a separate command: npm run web (Do NOT type npm start --w)

* For Android Emulator:
  - Press 'a' inside the running npm start terminal

